
// THE MAGMA FORM'S TAIL SWIPE - the two animations the last round could not tell apart.
// Converted from the OSRS cache by tools/models/animconvosrs.py; they play on their own base
// (base_osrs_5695), not the 377 one, so the client never walk-merges them with a 377 animation.
//
// WHICH OF 5806 AND 5807 IS THE TAIL. The answer below is the one the last round reached; the
// reasoning it reached it by was wrong, and it is replaced here rather than left standing, because
// a wrong derivation that happens to land on the right id is the thing that makes the NEXT id wrong.
//
// What the last round said was that 5806 "replays 18-26 and then 18,19,20 again - a hold loop", so
// 5806 waits and 5807 strikes. Both halves of that are mistaken. The replay of 18-26 and of 18,19,20
// is in the FIRST 35 FRAMES, which the two share frame for frame; it is the rear-up-and-stare the
// wiki describes ("Zulrah will stare at the player's position for several seconds before whipping
// its tail at that area"). AFTER it, both animations strike, into frames of their own that appear
// nowhere else on the rig, and then both recover through the same six frames:
//
//   5806  ... 28,29,30,31,32,31,30,29,28 ... 33,34,38,35,36,37,39
//   5807  ... 42,40,41,43,44,45,44,43,41,40,42,25 ... 34,38,35,36,37,39
//
// Two strikes, one wind-up, one recovery. Which one is a TAIL is not something a frame list can
// answer, so it was rendered: tools/models/posepreview.py on Zulrah's own mesh (OSRS npc 2042), the
// divergent frames of each, from in front at a fixed camera.
//
//   5806 brings the head DOWN AND FORWARD over the viewer with the hood spread symmetrically - a
//        lunging bite, straight at whatever is in front of it. It is not played. Nothing in this
//        fight bites.
//   5807 swings a long pale limb across the body from one side, out to full extension flat across
//        the frame, and back. That is the TAIL, and it is what the wiki says the red form does:
//        "a typeless attack wherein it swings its tail at the player's position".
//
// So 5807 it is, which is also what the private-server community publishes (melee target 5806,
// melee attack 5807, rune-server thread "Zulrah Animation/GFX Ids") - agreement worth noting and
// not worth leaning on, since that thread is where the last round's "target" reading came from.
//
// THE ANIMATION IS LONGER THAN THE BEAT, and this round the WARNING was moved to fit it rather than
// the other way round. 5807 is 200 client cycles at the cache's own delays, and its tail does not
// begin to come round until frame 35 - 140 cycles, 4.67 ticks. ^zulrah_melee_warning was 3, the
// wiki's attack speed, so the damage landed a second and a half before the tail on the screen moved.
// It is 5 now, which is where the swing actually is; zulrah.constant has the arithmetic. A second
// swipe still cuts the first one short, exactly as a long attack animation does on every other npc
// in this build.

[zulrah_tail_target]
// OSRS seq 5806 - the BITE, not the stare, whatever this name says. The name cannot be withdrawn
// (a packed name with no config throws in PackFile.ts), so it stays and the header says what the
// animation is. Not played: nothing in this fight bites.
reachforward=yes
priority=6
frame1=anim_osrs_5695_1
delay1=4
frame2=anim_osrs_5695_2
delay2=4
frame3=anim_osrs_5695_3
